WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.867
Eris, which made planet a definition.

00:03.567 --> 00:15.963
The definition astronomers agreed on in 2006 asks three things of a planet: it goes round the Sun, gravity has pulled it round, and it has cleared its own path.

00:16.413 --> 00:19.023
Eris and Pluto fail the third.

00:19.473 --> 00:27.345
Eris is near the far end of a 560-year lap, ninety five times as far from the Sun as we are.
